 # Building and publishing are separate jobs, so nothing that installs or builds can publish (alpha-build@1):
 # - build, with contents: read and no secrets, builds each apps/<app>/ present (npm ci --ignore-scripts,
 #   then npm run build with DEVTEAM_BASE_PATH=/next) and hands only its out/ on, as the artifact alpha.
+#   From layout 2 it builds each app again with DEVTEAM_BASE_PATH empty and hands that out/ on as the
+#   artifact apps, which the package carries in docs/devteam/apps/<app>/, served at the root.
 # - publish, with id-token: write in the npm-publish environment, installs and builds nothing: it runs
-#   test/release/package-check.mjs on the tag's checkout (the alpha's types, no dependencies, every kit file
-#   byte for byte the tag's, the version from the tag), then publishes the tarball that check packed. It
-#   reads no npm token: npm's trusted publisher for this file trusts the run by OIDC and makes the
-#   provenance itself.
-# - check, a third job that runs only on a pull request that changes this file, package.json, apps/ or
-#   test/release/: after build, the same package check with no publish rights, so the PR shows the packed
-#   file list in its run's summary. On a pull request publish is skipped; on a release, check is.
+#   test/release/package-check.mjs on the tag's checkout (the alpha's and the apps' types, no dependencies,
+#   the bin layout 2 names, every kit file byte for byte the tag's, the version from the tag), then
+#   publishes the tarball that check packed. It reads no npm token: npm's trusted publisher for this file
+#   trusts the run by OIDC and makes the provenance itself.
+# - deploy, after publish succeeds, calls box-deploy.yml as a reusable job (its only trigger): the
+#   called workflow sees this run's release event, its payload and its commit, so a minor deploys the box
+#   once, and only once its package is published. It passes the box's deploy hook by name, since GitHub
+#   gives a called workflow an environment's secret only when the caller passes it.
+# - check, a fourth job that runs only on a pull request that changes this file, box-deploy.yml,
+#   package.json, apps/ or test/release/: after build, the same package check with no publish rights, so the PR shows the packed
+#   file list in its run's summary. On a pull request publish and deploy are skipped; on a release, check is.
 #
 # The owner's one-time setup, before the first release that carries this file:
 # 1. In this repository's settings, the environment npm-publish, limited to tags matching v*: a run
